<%# The board tile's title, in display mode. Lives in its OWN frame (nested
    inside the tile's card frame) so the tile's pencil can swap just this for an
    inline edit form without disturbing the rest of the tile. Deliberately not
    the same frame id as the modal's title: the modal opens over the board, so
    both can be on the page at once — see CardsController#title_context.

    `flex-1 min-w-0` sits on the frame itself, since the frame IS the flex child
    of the title row now (it took the old link's place). A bare <turbo-frame>
    defaults to display:inline, but a flex item is blockified regardless, so no
    explicit `block` is needed here — unlike the tile's outer frame, whose
    vertical margin depends on it. min-w-0 is what keeps a long title (and the
    edit field that replaces it) from pushing the tile wider than its column. %>
<%= turbo_frame_tag dom_id(card, :tile_title), class: "flex-1 min-w-0" do %>
  <%# Clicking the title still opens the modal, exactly as before — only the
      pencil enters edit mode. data-turbo-frame="modal" overrides this frame. %>
  <%= link_to card_path(card),
      data: { turbo_frame: "modal" },
      class: "block no-underline text-inherit" do %>
    <h4 class="text-sm font-medium text-ink-700 leading-tight"><%= card.title %></h4>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
